    "original": {
      "label": "原文",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Today we identified a security incident involving a specific extension package in the Cursor VS Code extension Marketplace: Anthropic.claude-code version 2.1.313. This malicious version of the extension was not developed by Anthropic. At most 4,100 users were affected, and we will reach out directly.",
          "inlines": [
            {
              "text": "Today we identified a security incident involving a specific extension package in the Cursor VS Code extension Marketplace: "
            },
            {
              "bold": true,
              "text": "Anthropic.claude-code version 2.1.313"
            },
            {
              "text": ". This malicious version of the extension was not developed by Anthropic. At most 4,100 users were affected, and we will reach out directly."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What happened",
          "inlines": [
            {
              "text": "What happened"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Between about 2:27am PT and 1:35pm PT today, a maliciously modified version of Anthropic’s Claude Code extension was made available in the Cursor VS Code extension Marketplace. The extension runs malicious code that attempts to install a persistent SSH backdoor. Specifically, it:",
          "inlines": [
            {
              "text": "Between about 2:27am PT and 1:35pm PT today, a maliciously modified version of Anthropic’s Claude Code extension was made available in the Cursor VS Code extension Marketplace. The extension runs malicious code that attempts to install a persistent SSH backdoor. Specifically, it:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            {
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "text": "Collects host and user information: hostname, username, OS, architecture, home directory path, environment variable names, working directories, configured Git email, and public IP."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "text": "Attempts to add an attacker-controlled SSH key to "
                },
                {
                  "code": true,
                  "text": "authorized_keys"
                },
                {
                  "text": ", enable the local SSH service, and open a reverse SSH tunnel. Outside of highly unusual circumstances where Cursor was started with administrator privileges, due to errors in the malicious code, this step would fail."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "text": "Attempts to make the reverse SSH tunnel persistent via a LaunchAgent (macOS) or a scheduled task that attempts to run as SYSTEM with a Startup-script fallback (Windows). Background scripts retry the tunnel roughly every 60 seconds."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "text": "Reports host details and backdoor status via HTTP POST to "
                },
                {
                  "code": true,
                  "text": "/beacon"
                },
                {
                  "text": " on port 8099."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Note: The attacker server no longer functions.",
          "inlines": [
            {
              "bold": true,
              "text": "Note: The attacker server no longer functions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            {
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "text": "We worked with the cloud provider that was hosting it to take it offline, so the reverse shell and host detail POST are not functional."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "text": "These findings concern the identified package. We have no evidence that other versions of the extension or the official distribution are affected."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "text": "Additionally, turning on the local SSH service requires admin rights, which the malicious extension does not have on most macOS and Windows hosts. On those hosts the step fails and the attacker could not have logged in through the tunnel. The extension still adds the attacker’s SSH key, installs persistence, and sends host details to the attacker. Follow the remediation steps below regardless."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What we did",
          "inlines": [
            {
              "text": "What we did"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            {
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "text": "Removed the malicious version from the marketplace immediately upon detection and blocked further distribution. We followed with a full shut down of the VSCode Marketplace out of an abundance of caution."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "text": "We audited access and confirmed no other extensions were tampered with."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "text": "We rotated our keys, rebuilt the marketplace, and brought it back online"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "text": "We worked with the hosting provider to take the malicious server offline, disrupting the attack by blocking the connection to that server."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What you should do",
          "inlines": [
            {
              "text": "What you should do"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "If you installed or updated to Anthropic.claude-code 2.1.313 from Cursor VS Code extension marketplace between 2:27am PT and 1:35pm PT on October 29, 2026:",
          "inlines": [
            {
              "text": "If you installed or updated to Anthropic.claude-code 2.1.313 from Cursor VS Code extension marketplace between 2:27am PT and 1:35pm PT on October 29, 2026:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": true,
          "items": [
            {
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "text": "Run the check below to validate if you are impacted."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "text": "Search across endpoint, network, and extension-installation telemetry for the indicators below."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "text": "Isolate hosts showing evidence of payload execution or backdoor installation."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "text": "Remove the unauthorized SSH key, persistence mechanisms, and running tunnel processes using the remediation scripts below, and assess whether the host should be rebuilt. Uninstalling the extension may not be sufficient — the payload drops standalone persistence scripts that keep running."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "text": "Rotate credentials and sessions accessible from affected hosts, from a trusted system. The limited env-var collection does not rule out later credential access over the backdoor."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Check whether you are impacted",
          "inlines": [
            {
              "text": "Check whether you are impacted"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The malicious extension appends the attacker's public key, labeled svc-telemetry, to your SSH authorized keys. To check for it:",
          "inlines": [
            {
              "text": "The malicious extension appends the attacker's public key, labeled "
            },
            {
              "code": true,
              "text": "svc-telemetry"
            },
            {
              "text": ", to your SSH authorized keys. To check for it:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "On macOS, run:",
          "inlines": [
            {
              "text": "On macOS, run:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "grep -qs svc-telemetry ~/.ssh/authorized_keys && echo \"svc-telemetry key found\" || echo \"No key found; machine not impacted\""
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "On Windows, run in PowerShell:",
          "inlines": [
            {
              "text": "On Windows, run in PowerShell:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "$files = \"$HOME\\.ssh\\authorized_keys\", \"C:\\ProgramData\\ssh\\administrators_authorized_keys\" | Where-Object { Test-Path $_ }\nif ($files -and (Select-String svc-telemetry $files)) { \"svc-telemetry key found\" } else { \"No key found; machine not impacted\" }"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "If the key is found, your machine is impacted. Follow steps 3 to 5 above, and run the remediation script for your platform below.",
          "inlines": [
            {
              "text": "If the key is found, your machine is impacted. Follow steps 3 to 5 above, and run the remediation script for your platform below."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "These scripts remove the malicious extension, the persistence mechanisms, the running tunnel processes, and the attacker's SSH key. They exit with a non-zero status if anything remains.",
          "inlines": [
            {
              "text": "These scripts remove the malicious extension, the persistence mechanisms, the running tunnel processes, and the attacker's SSH key. They exit with a non-zero status if anything remains."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "On macOS, download remediate-macos.sh and run it as the affected user, not as root, from the folder you saved it to:",
          "inlines": [
            {
              "text": "On macOS, download "
            },
            {
              "href": "https://cursor.com/static/security/claude-code-extension/remediate-macos.sh",
              "text": "remediate-macos.sh"
            },
            {
              "text": " and run it as the affected user, not as root, from the folder you saved it to:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "bash remediate-macos.sh"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "On Windows, download remediate-windows.ps1 and run it from PowerShell opened with Run as Administrator, in the folder you saved it to:",
          "inlines": [
            {
              "text": "On Windows, download "
            },
            {
              "href": "https://cursor.com/static/security/claude-code-extension/remediate-windows.ps1",
              "text": "remediate-windows.ps1"
            },
            {
              "text": " and run it from PowerShell opened with "
            },
            {
              "bold": true,
              "text": "Run as Administrator"
            },
            {
              "text": ", in the folder you saved it to:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\\remediate-windows.ps1"
        },
